  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{25{y}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{16}=4$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.$",
